From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Graham Taylor-Jones <graham.taylor-jones@cargt.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:28:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: imx93-cargt-00363-osm-som: hog PMIC_IRQ_B to
 input

gpio1 pin 10 (PMIC_IRQ_B, pmic@25's interrupt line) can come up with
GDIR already set to output before Linux boots (SoC POR default or the
M33/ELE firmware stage - not U-Boot's board code, which never touches
this pin). gpiochip_lock_as_irq() reads live hardware direction at
request time for this non-sleeping SoC-native gpiochip and refuses to
use an output-configured line for IRQ, so nxp-pca9450's probe fails
with -EIO ("tried to flag a GPIO set as output for IRQ"), taking BUCK1
(and anything depending on it, e.g. imx93-lpm) down with it.

Hog the line to input at gpiochip registration time, well before
pmic@25 probes, regardless of what set it wrong.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board specific]
---
 .../dts/freescale/imx93-cargt-00363-osm-som.dts | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx93-cargt-00363-osm-som.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx93-cargt-00363-osm-som.dts
index c09ce2b12803..35936a9fe6ba 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx93-cargt-00363-osm-som.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx93-cargt-00363-osm-som.dts
@@ -116,6 +116,23 @@ &gpio1{
 	"gpio1-20","gpio1-21","gpio1-22","gpio1-23", 	// 20-23
 	"gpio1-24","gpio1-25","gpio1-26","gpio1-27", 	// 24-27
 	"gpio1-28","gpio1-29","gpio1-30","gpio1-31"; 	// 28-31
+
+	/*
+	 * PMIC_IRQ_B (pmic@25's interrupt line, MX93_PAD_PDM_BIT_STREAM1__GPIO1_IO10)
+	 * comes up with GDIR already set to output from before Linux boots (SoC
+	 * POR default or the M33/ELE firmware stage - not U-Boot, its board code
+	 * never touches this pin). gpiochip_lock_as_irq() reads live hardware
+	 * direction at request time for this non-sleeping SoC-native gpiochip and
+	 * refuses to use an output-configured line for IRQ, so pca9450's probe
+	 * fails with -EIO ("tried to flag a GPIO set as output for IRQ"). Hog it
+	 * to input here, at gpiochip registration time, well before pmic@25 probes.
+	 */
+	pmic-irq-hog {
+		gpio-hog;
+		gpios = <10 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+		input;
+		line-name = "PMIC_IRQ_B";
+	};
 };
 
 &gpio2{
